         MODTRAN 3.5 VERSION 1.1 USER INSTRUCTIONS & COMMENTS  (1/97)

	MODTRAN (all versions) is patented software that may not be sold or 
used in commercial software without prior arrangements with the U.S. government 
regarding licensing procedures. MODTRAN (all versions) may only be 
released by Phillips Laboratory in order to assure continuing contact with the 
user community.

	A signed copy of the MODTRAN 3.5 Non-Disclosure Agreement in file 
m3.5-non-disclosure needs to be faxed to Gail Anderson at "ganderson@plh.af.mil". 
You will receive instructions for ftping the code from the pasword ftp site. The 
password for the ftp site is changed each Monday. 

	Upgrades to MODTRAN 3.5 will be put on the anonymous ftp site in directory 
mod3.5-changes. Check the anonymous ftp site at the beginning of the month for 
upgrades. Users will receive notice of major upgrades. The anonymous ftp site will 
have the latest Readme file and a complete Documentation.dir, Changes.dir, and 
Case.dir. Only the modified source files will be in Source.dir/SOURCE, as opposed
to the full source code which is only available on the password ftp site. The
bandmodel in DATA will not be on the anonymous ftp site.

	Questions or other communications can be sent to:
	Gail Anderson - 'ganderson@plh.af.mil', 1st query and CC's of all questions
	Jim Chetwynd - 'chetwynd@plh.af.mil' , user implementation, templates, PC, etc.
	Julia Vail - 'vail@pldac.plh.af.mil', installation, platform conversions, etc.
	Lex Berk - 'lex@spectral.com', MOD3.5 specifics (band model & clouds, etc.)
  
	For each new version of MODTRAN 3.5, there will be two files listing changes in 
the subdirectory 'Changes.dir'. 'code-*.*' will list the coding changes with the 
'*.*' referring to the version number. 'updates-*.*' will specify general changes 
similar to this information . Any significant changes to the 'Readme' file will 
also be noted in the 'updates*.*' file.

	Subdirectory Documentation.dir contains user instructions, 
'refbkg.doc' which describes how to add user defined backgrounds to refbkg, 
and the paper 'FASCODE/MODTRAN.LOWTRAN: Past/Present/Future' with the text in 
'paper.*' and the figures in 'figures.*' The files 'cloud.*' contains user 
instructions for the new cloud models supplementing the MODTRAN 3.0 user 
instructions in files 'modtrn3.wp6*'. Here is a listing of the paper titles.

------------------------ cloud (.asc, .ps, .wp51, .wp6): ---------------------------

