		RUNNING THE MODTRAN 3.5 EXECUTABLE

	There are four files that need to be in the path of the executable 
MODTRAN 3.5 in directory 'DATA': 'MOLBMP96.BIN', 'CFCBMP96.ASC', 'sun_kur.dat' 
and 'refbkg'. 'MOLBMP96.BIN' is the binary band model file.  'CFCBMP96.ASC', the 
band model tape for the CFC's, is sufficiently small as not to require being 
converted into binary from ascii format. 'sun_kur.dat' contains the 1 cm-1 
"binned" solar irradiance data, and 'refbkg' contains the surface albedos for 
ten background types: fresh snow cover, forest, farm, desert, ocean, cloud 
deck, maple leaf and 3 grass models.

 	MODTRAN 3.5 is not an interactive code. It reads the input parameters 
from a file named 'tape5' and writes output to the files 'tape6', 'tape7', 
and the optional 'tape8' and 'plot.dat'. There are test cases in the directory 
'Case.dir'. Use each ***.tp5 file as a test input tape5 and compare the tape6 
with the given ***.tp6 file. A new test case, 'cld1.tp5', is an example of 
how to use the new cloud parameters.

		TAPE5 INPUT CARD CHANGES

	The tape5 format for MODTRAN 3.0 without clouds should be compatible 
with MODTRAN 3.5. 'Documentation.dir/cloud.*' describes the input changes for 
cloud specifications. 

	The modifications to the SUN1 and ISUN parameters in card 1b are descibed 
in 'Documentation.dir/m3.5-upgrade.*'. 

	(Q) SOLAR SPECTRUM
	    The use of the solar irradiance function inputs SUN1 and ISUN (CARD1A) 
	    has been modified.

	    If SUN1 is .FALSE.,
        	 solar irradiances are obtained from a block data containing
         	KURUCZ data degraded to 5 cm-1 (FWHM triangular slit) resolution
         	and tabulated each cm-1.

	    If SUN1 is .TRUE.,
        	 KURUCZ data from the file sun_kur.dat (formerly "sun2") is
        	 degraded to |ISUN| cm-1 (FWHM triangular slit) resolution and
        	 tabulated each cm-1.  If ISUN is negative, the resulting data
        	 is output to file "sun####.dat", where #### is the resolution.



	A new output file for plotting, 'plot.dat' that can be requested and defined 
on card 4 is also described in 'Documentation.dir/m3.5-upgrade.*'.

	(P) PLOT OUTPUT FILE
	    MODTRAN 3.5 allows the user to create a plot (x vs y) output file, 
	"plot.dat".
	This file is defined using three new CARD 4 inputs, YFLAG, XFLAG and DLIMIT

	    READ(IPR,'(4I10,2A1,A8)')IV1,IV2,IDV,IFWHM,YFLAG,XFLAG,DLIMIT

	    If YFLAG is 'T' or 't', transmittances are output;
	    If YFLAG is 'R' or 'r', radiances are output 
		(irradiances if IEMSCT=3);   
	    Otherwise, no plot.dat file is created.

	    If XFLAG is 'M' or 'm', wavelengths are in um and radiances are in 
		W SR-1 CM-2 / um;
	    If XFLAG is 'N' or 'n', wavelengths are in NM and radiances are in 
		uW SR-1 CM-2 / NM;
	    Otherwise, frequencies are in CM-1 and radiances are in 
		W SR-1 CM-2 / CM-1.
    
	    DLIMIT is the delimiter written between MODTRAN runs (IRPT>0).

	If DLIMIT is blank, no separation is inserted between MODTRAN runs.  If a
	delimiter is used, then the minimum and maximum transmittance/radiance is
	written on the delimiter line.


